# Single-instance-only local override file for ds-image.
#
# IMPORTANT: if this service ever shares a Tomcat instance with other WARs (as the development server does,
# running all 6 ds-backend services in one Tomcat), do NOT use this file for devops/operations secrets - use
# conf/ds-image-application.properties.SAMPLE instead. The reason: this file is picked up via SmallRye Config's
# own implicit 'config/application.properties' convention (ordinal 260), keyed off the JVM's current working
# directory - which every webapp in that shared Tomcat instance has in common, so there is no way for this file
# to affect only ds-image. A file left here would silently apply to every service sharing that Tomcat instance.
# conf/ds-image-application.properties is instead read from an explicit, per-service path configured via its own
# Tomcat context environment entry, so it cannot leak across services.
#
# This file is only safe to use for a single, standalone instance of the service (e.g. running it alone via an
# IDE, or 'java -jar', from a working directory nothing else shares) - copy it to 'config/application.properties'
# (same folder, without the '.SAMPLE' suffix) and fill in your own values; no code change and no extra argument
# to ServiceConfig.initialize(...) is needed for it to apply, since addDefaultSources() already registers it.
#
# 'config/application.properties' is (and must stay) git-ignored; see .gitignore.
#
# Any key present in ds-image-behaviour.yaml can be overridden here, using the same dotted path. The keys below
# are the ones commonly set per environment/operator - uncomment and set the ones you need.
#
# IMPORTANT: the imageservers.* keys are NOT present in ds-image-behaviour.yaml at all - one of the two Deepzoom
# variants (path- or param-based) plus iip and iiif must be supplied here (or elsewhere) for the service to work.

# imageservers.iip.server=http://example.com:1234/iipsrv/iipsrv.fcgi
# imageservers.iiif.server=http://example.com:1234/
# imageservers.deepzoom.path=http://example.com:1234/
# imageservers.deepzoom.param=http://example.com:1234/iipsrv/iipsrv.fcgi

# kaltura.partnerId=380
# kaltura.userId=changeme
# kaltura.adminSecret=changeme

# security.client.secret=changeme

# openapi.serverurl=http://localhost:9077/ds-image/v1
